cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "meshfind: offline, end-to-end encrypted Find-My network over an ESP32 mesh"
authors:
  - name: "the meshfind authors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/coopersimpson101-debug/meshfind"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  An offline, end-to-end encrypted crowd-sourced finding network for DIY BLE trackers, relayed over an ESP32 ESP-NOW mesh: rotating X25519 keys from a one-way HKDF ratchet, ECIES location reports with ChaCha20-Poly1305, gradient mesh routing, indoor trilateration and anti-stalking detection, with a Python reference implementation and a byte-identical portable C core.
keywords:
  - BLE
  - ESP32
  - mesh networking
  - cryptography
  - X25519
  - privacy
  - offline finding
  - anti-stalking
